# goal Translate between two shapes, and nothing else

Everything in this file is a pure function of its arguments. That is what makes the
OpenAI surface testable without spawning an agent or opening a socket, and it is the
property to protect when adding to it.

# invariant No I/O, ever {#pure}

No filesystem, no network, no clock beyond what callers pass in, no `process.env`.
`created` timestamps and completion ids are produced by `newCompletionId()` and by
the caller respectively, so responses stay reproducible in tests.

The rule bites hardest on attachments: a remote `image_url` or a `file_id` is
**refused, never fetched**. Fetching would make a translation function egress —
silently, from wherever this is deployed, which in the original deployment is behind
a VPN on purpose.

# func toPromptBlocks {#to_prompt}

Renders OpenAI `messages` into ACP content blocks.

## arg messages
The OpenAI array. Rejected when empty, when a message lacks `role`, or when it
contains only system messages.

## result
`[{type: "text", text}, ...attachments]` — always exactly one text block first,
followed by image and resource blocks in the order they appeared.

## flow
1. Flatten each message's content, collecting attachments as ACP blocks.
2. Split into system/developer messages and conversation turns.
3. A **single** turn is passed through verbatim — the common case must not be
   wrapped in scaffolding the model then has to see through.
4. Several turns become a labelled `User:` / `Assistant:` transcript, which is the
   only faithful option when the agent owns its own conversation state.
5. System text is prepended, unlabelled.

## invariant A one-turn request produces the user's text unchanged
Any added prefix, suffix or label on the single-turn path is a regression, however
harmless it looks.

# func makeLimiter {#limiter}

Builds the callback `Agent.prompt` consults after each chunk. Returns `null` when
the request asks for no limits, so the hot path stays free of a no-op call.

## result
`null`, or `(text) => null | {stopReason, text}`.

## invariant The limiter is pure and idempotent
It is called after every chunk with the full accumulated text, so it must decide
from that text alone and never from call history. See
[_.hint#param_policy](../_.hint) for why only `stop` and `max_tokens` qualify.

## rule A stop sequence is excluded from the answer
OpenAI semantics: the text is cut **before** the match, and the reason is
`end_turn` — the model stopped where it was told to, it did not run out.

# data estimateTokens {#token_estimate}

`Math.ceil(text.length / 4)`. Deliberately crude and documented as such: the agent
picks the model, so no tokenizer here can be correct. `max_tokens` is a budget, not
an accountant. Do not replace this with a real tokenizer without also deciding which
model's tokenizer it is supposed to be.

# rule Response builders never invent fields {#response_shape}

`completion`, `chunk` and `usageChunk` emit exactly what OpenAI emits, plus
`reasoning_content` and `x_acp2api` — both omitted entirely when empty rather than
sent as `""` or `[]`. An unknown future ACP stop reason maps to `"stop"`, never to
an invalid `finish_reason` that a strict client would reject.

# test openai

- a single user turn passes through with no scaffolding
- system and developer messages are prepended, not labelled
- a multi-turn history becomes a labelled transcript
- content part arrays flatten; data-URI images become image blocks
- `file`/`input_file` parts become resource blocks: text inline, binary as blob
- `file_id` and remote `image_url` are refused rather than fetched
- malformed requests (no messages, no role, system-only, no model) are rejected
- `parseChatRequest` surfaces `stream`, `includeUsage`, `maxTokens`, `stop`, `ignored`
- `max_completion_tokens` wins over `max_tokens`; both validated as positive integers
- `makeLimiter` returns null when unconstrained; cuts before a stop sequence; truncates on budget
- stop reasons map to `finish_reason`, and an unknown one maps to `"stop"`
- `reasoning_content` and `x_acp2api` are absent, not empty, when there is nothing to report
- usage maps ACP token names to OpenAI's, including reasoning tokens
